":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the plan with the existing prior art: cite infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md's 'GitHub Actions mirror sync' section (and tests/unit/test_secret_rotation_runbook.py), state which ACs it already satisfies, and re-scope the work to the genuine delta (e.g. cross-linking from the ROTATE step, adding a rotation-ordering guarantee, or the drift check) rather than re-authoring the inventory/commands.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4281,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md lines 83-124 contain the '### GitHub Actions mirror sync' section: an inventory table (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> /rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key, JIRA_API_TOKEN -> /rebar/prod/jira-api-token, GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY -> /rebar/prod/ci-gerrit-ssh-key, OPENAI_API_KEY -> 'GitHub-only', REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY -> /rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key), per-secret `aws ssm get-parameter ... | gh secret set` commands, and an optional 'compare LastModifiedDate vs gh secret list --json name,updatedAt' drift check.","AC1 ('inventory maps each GitHub Actions secret to its SSM source or marks it GitHub-only, in the ops runbook under infra/runbooks/') is already satisfied by that table; AC2 ('explicit GitHub Actions sync step (gh secret set from SSM) with a copy-paste command per mapped secret') by lines 100-116; AC3 (optional drift check) by lines 121-124.","tests/unit/test_secret_rotation_runbook.py lines 7-33 assert the exact inventory rows and the exact `gh secret set` / `aws ssm get-parameter` commands, showing the procedure is already implemented and covered.","ABSENCE: the plan's Context and Acceptance Criteria never mention ssm-secret-write-only.md, its 'GitHub Actions mirror sync' section, or the existing test — no prior-art consideration is recorded.","External prior art retrieved via search corroborates this is a well-trodden pattern (AWS Secrets Manager 'Use secrets in GitHub jobs' docs; 'AWS SSM Sync Parameters' / 'AWS SSM Build Secrets' GitHub Marketplace actions), reinforcing that the mechanism is established rather than novel."],"finding":"The plan proposes an SSM->GitHub Actions secret-sync inventory, per-secret `gh secret set` commands, and an optional drift check that already exist, near-verbatim, in the repo's SSM rotation runbook (infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md) and are locked in by tests (tests/unit/test_secret_rotation_runbook.py). The plan considers no prior art and does not reference the existing runbook/section, so as written it reinvents shipped functionality.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc98b39b23fb3e69d","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Whole plan / Acceptance Criteria (AC1, AC2, AC3)","norm_id":"n3b28462f1bcfad68","priority":0.3719,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer follows the plan and adds a second, competing inventory/sync section in a different runbook, creating two sources of truth that can drift.","The author is unaware AC1/AC2/AC3 are already met and spends effort re-deriving the table and commands."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explana